### Description

Currently there is no way to detect errors that happened during streaming when using `readUIMessageStream`, the message generator will just stop yielding new messages

Instead it should throw an error when it encounters an error stream part, for example it should throw an error when the UIStream contains something like this:

```
{
  "type": "error",
  "errorText": "Invalid input for tool strReplaceEditor: Type validation failed: Value: {"command":"str_replace","path":"essentials/images.md","old_str":"<img\n  style={{ borderRadius: '0.5rem' }}\n  src=\"https://uploads.fumabase.com/Gui86K8XoAAZRb_.jpeg\"\n/>\n\n","new_str":""}.
Error message: [
  {
    "expected": "string",
    "code": "invalid_type",
    "path": [
      "file_text"
    ],
    "message": "Invalid input: expected string, received undefined"
  },
  {
    "expected": "number",
    "code": "invalid_type",
    "path": [
      "insert_line"
    ],
    "message": "Invalid input: expected number, received undefined"
  },
  {
    "expected": "array",
    "code": "invalid_type",
    "path": [
      "view_range"
    ],
    "message": "Invalid input: expected array, received undefined"
  }
]"
}


```

